"stopped trading, or that a :class:`pybroker.common.SymbolSelector` "
"dropped -- whose prices would otherwise raise."
msgstr ""

#: 9eda7b7e811246c2a0a96e56375c3931 of pybroker.scope.PriceScope.has_bar_on:1
msgid "Returns whether ``symbol``'s current bar falls on ``date``."
msgstr ""

#: cb0d7983daba419b8a860931845f4213 of pybroker.scope.PriceScope.has_bar_on:3
msgid ""
"Stricter than :meth:`.has_bar`, which only reports that the symbol has "
"traded at some point. When calendars are ragged, a symbol's index is not "
"advanced on a date it has no bar, so its \"current\" bar is an earlier "
"one and pricing against it would use a stale price."
msgstr ""

#: 4ed9d2191b1d49e6a1e9192bdc05f655 of pybroker.scope.PriceScope.has_bar_on:8
msgid ""
"Memoized per bar: ``check_stops`` calls this once per symbol holding a "
"stop on every bar, and each miss fetches the symbol's whole date array. "
"Keyed by date as well as symbol so a caller that does not call "
":meth:`.reset_bar` still reads a correct answer."
msgstr ""

#: ff675a1060024602b5571d9e8a6e79bc of pybroker.scope.PriceScope.reset_bar:1
msgid "Clears the per-bar OHLC cache. Call once at the start of each bar."
msgstr ""

